# Force LF on checkout regardless of the checking-out machine's own
# core.autocrlf — discovered as a real bug via Prompt 15's Windows CI run:
# GitHub's windows-latest runners default core.autocrlf=true, which was
# silently rewriting every committed text file's line endings to CRLF on
# checkout with no .gitattributes here to override it. That broke content-
# hash manifest verification for every packaged fixture (project.json's
# checked-out byte count no longer matched its manifest-declared size/hash)
# — the exact class of bug this project's own CLAUDE.md calls out as a
# first-class test case, just not yet exercised on real Windows until now.
# A real Windows contributor with Git for Windows' own default
# core.autocrlf=true would have hit the identical corruption locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binary formats — never subject to any line-ending processing, even
# under text=auto's own (generally reliable, but not infallible) heuristic
# detection. .fdstudio/.fdtheme are packaged ZIP archives whose content-hash
# manifest verification depends on exact byte-for-byte integrity.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.fdstudio binary
*.fdtheme binary
*.zip binary
